learn=[('Connect the official docs server', 'The HTTP experiment connects to the live Claude Code documentation MCP endpoint. The agent calls its real search tool and cites a returned source. Feedback submission is excluded by the host guard.'), ('Launch an external stdio process', 'The SDK launches the pinned official filesystem server using Node and an argument array. Only a fresh classroom folder is supplied as its allowed root. This is a separate process, unlike an in-process SDK server.'), ('Load a project .mcp.json', 'Compare inline mcpServers with a real generated .mcp.json. The project experiment enables settingSources: ["project"] and explicitly approves the controlled project server. The application’s real .env is outside that folder.'), ('Name and approve tools', 'Inspect actual mcp__ tool names. Compare an exact filesystem approval with an unapproved second call. The combined experiment also demonstrates a docs wildcard, limited to search by a separate host guard.'), ('Distinguish permissions from availability', 'acceptEdits does not pre-approve these MCP calls. This app denies unresolved permission requests and records what was attempted and completed. It does not use bypassPermissions.'), ('Observe actual connection state', 'Inspect mcp_servers at initialization and later mcpServerStatus() results. The startup experiment adds a labelled two-second server delay and an explicit wait setting. Measurements describe this run, not a universal startup time.')]
document('/','Connect <em>external MCP.</em>','Real stdio processes, remote HTTP servers and observable connection state.','<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Declare</b><p>Code or project configuration</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Connect</b><p>stdio command or HTTP URL</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Approve</b><p>Actual names, calls and status</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><h2>Connect real external MCP servers</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta">Checking local server…</p><label for="mode">External-MCP experiment</label><select id="mode"><option value="docs-http">HTTP · official Claude Code docs</option><option value="stdio-code">stdio · filesystem declared in code</option><option value="stdio-config">Project config · actual .mcp.json</option><option value="combined">Same session · filesystem + docs HTTP</option><option value="exact-approval">Exact approval · deny a second tool</option><option value="accept-edits">acceptEdits · no MCP pre-approval</option><option value="startup-wait">Connection timing · controlled startup delay</option></select><button id="run" class="primary" disabled>Run external-MCP experiment →</button><p class="meta">The docs endpoint is a real remote service. The filesystem server is a real external child process with a fresh classroom root. The host guard permits only docs search and directory listing; no feedback, file edits or unrelated actions.</p></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><p>SDK reported cost: <strong id="cost">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Session: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Compare mcpServers, settingSources, strictMcpConfig, allowedTools and permissionMode. Project config is loaded deliberately; the other experiments use code-only declarations.</p></section></div><section class="step" id="configuration-panel"><h2>Inspect actual server configuration</h2><label for="configuration-file">Configuration or fixture</label><select id="configuration-file"></select><pre class="json-view"><code id="configuration-content" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>These are the actual generated classroom fixtures and server declarations. The .mcp.json variant is written into the fresh project. It contains no real API key; the external filesystem process receives a blank ANTHROPIC_API_KEY value.</p></section><section class="step" id="discovery-panel"><h2>Discover actual MCP names at initialization</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="discovery" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="connection-panel"><h2>Actual connection status after initialization</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="connections" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>mcpServerStatus() is polled for up to fifteen seconds when a server is pending. The app preserves initialization status separately. A later connected result does not mean the server was already connected at init.</p></section><section class="step" id="native-panel"><h2>Actual SDK tool-result projection</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="native" class="language-json">[]</code></pre><p>Directory results come from the actual official filesystem process. Search results come from the real documentation MCP service. Long text is shortened in this projection; no saved answer replaces a live response.</p></section><section class="step" id="evidence-panel"><h2>Verify calls, approvals and connection timing</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="evidence" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Completed calls are recorded separately from permission requests. Fixture comparisons verify the original classroom files remain unchanged. Timing includes runtime startup and actual connection work, so it is not a benchmark.</p></section><section class="step" id="init-panel"><h2>Actual system/init projection</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="init" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="run-history"><h2>Compare this browser’s experiments</h2><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Connected servers</th><th>Completed calls</th><th>Callback requests</th><th>Init elapsed</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div><button id="download">Download actual observations</button></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Actual SDK messages</h2><ol id="events"></ol></section>','<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
document('/learn.html','What you <em>will learn.</em>','Connect tools from the MCP ecosystem and verify their actual calls.',cards(learn))
env='ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key\nCLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6\nPORT=3124\n# Optional on Windows: CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe'
runsteps=[('Prepare Node and model access', 'Use Node.js 24 or later and a funded model API account. On Windows the SDK may require Git Bash. The HTTP docs server needs internet access. The official filesystem server is pinned and installed with this app.', 'node --version\nnpm --version'), ('Install and create your .env file', 'From presentations run these commands. Preserve an existing .env, enter the API key privately and restart after changes. Existing shell values take precedence.', 'cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson24-external-mcp\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env'), ('Start the web application', 'Keep this terminal running. The Agent SDK launches the external filesystem process when needed; you do not start it manually. Ctrl+C stops the web application.', 'npm start\n# http://127.0.0.1:3124'), ('Search the real docs and list a classroom folder', 'Run the HTTP and stdio experiments. Inspect actual fully qualified tool names, connection status and returned sources or filenames. The allowed root is a fresh classroom folder, not your entire computer.', 'npm run sample:env -- docs-http\nnpm run sample:env -- stdio-code'), ('Load project config and combine transports', 'Project mode writes and loads an actual .mcp.json with project settings enabled. Combined mode connects both real servers in one session. No manual config edit is required for the classroom exercise.', 'npm run sample:env -- stdio-config\nnpm run sample:env -- combined'), ('Compare approval and connection timing', 'Exact approval allows directory listing but denies an unapproved second tool. acceptEdits has no MCP pre-approval. Startup mode labels a two-second wrapper delay and reports actual elapsed initialization time.', 'npm run sample:env -- exact-approval\nnpm run sample:env -- accept-edits\nnpm run sample:env -- startup-wait\nnpm test')]
body=''
for i,(title,explanation,code) in enumerate(runsteps,1):body+=f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{explanation}</p>'+snippet(code,'powershell')+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Your .env configuration</h2>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>Keep the actual key private. No Managed Agents agent ID or environment ID is required. No duplicate snapshot is included.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>Use the URL printed by startup. If another app occupies the port, change PORT and restart. If API credit is unavailable, add credit to the account used by this key. MCP connection failures remain visible; no saved response replaces a failed live call. The CLI experiments use the same local key and pinned server dependencies.</p></section>'
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the app.</em>','Install the SDK, configure your key and connect external tools.',body)
specs=[('Validate the experiment', 'src/external.ts', 'return { mode:', 'Accept one of the seven fixed tasks. The browser cannot supply arbitrary server commands, URLs or filesystem roots.', 0, 1), ('Declare the stdio command', 'src/external.ts', 'command: process.execPath,', 'Launch the pinned official filesystem server with an argument array and only the owned classroom root. The real model API key is not supplied to that process.', 1, 3), ('Declare the HTTP server', 'src/external.ts', 'const docs: McpServerConfig =', 'Connect to the real Claude Code docs MCP URL. This is an external HTTP service, distinct from both local stdio and an in-process SDK server.', 1, 3), ('Write the project config', 'src/external.ts', 'if (mode === "stdio-config")', 'Write an actual .mcp.json into the fresh classroom project. Its filesystem server points only to that controlled folder.', 1, 2), ('Enable the project setting source', 'src/agent.ts', 'settingSources: project ?', 'The .mcp.json experiment includes the project source and explicitly approves its controlled project server. strictMcpConfig is disabled only for that experiment so project declarations can load.', 1, 2), ('Approve the intended tool names', 'src/external.ts', 'if (mode === "docs-http")', 'Use a fully qualified name for the docs search or a wildcard in the combined experiment. The separate host guard narrows actual actions to search and classroom listing.', 1, 2), ('Start the real SDK query', 'src/agent.ts', 'const run = query(', 'Pass the chosen server declarations to query. The SDK spawns stdio processes or opens remote MCP connections and orchestrates model calls.', 1, 2), ('Preserve initialization status', 'src/agent.ts', 'initServers = message.mcp_servers.map', 'Initialization is a snapshot. Preserve the reported connection statuses and elapsed time instead of assuming every configured server has connected.', 2, 1), ('Poll current server state', 'src/agent.ts', 'connectedServers = (await run.mcpServerStatus())', 'Poll actual current status when needed and keep it distinct from the initialization snapshot. Tool lists and configuration source are visible when supplied by the runtime.', 1, 2), ('Observe the requested tool call', 'src/agent.ts', 'if (block.type === "tool_use")', 'Inspect the actual model-requested MCP name and arguments. A discovered tool or prose answer alone does not establish successful execution.', 4, 2), ('Enforce the classroom boundary', 'src/agent.ts', 'attempts.push(input.tool_name);', 'The pre-tool hook records attempts and rejects unrelated operations. Native SDK permission rules and the callback then determine approval for allowed classroom targets.', 2, 1), ('Record actual completion', 'src/agent.ts', 'if (input.hook_event_name === "PostToolUse")', 'PostToolUse records completed calls separately from attempts and callback denials. Directory output comes from the external process and docs output from the real remote server.', 3, 2), ('Render answers with evidence', 'src/client.ts', 'if (e.type === "answer")', 'Format and sanitize actual Markdown, including documentation links. Keep it beside actual connection status, permissions and tool-result evidence.', 1, 0)]
steps=[];arrows=[];lanes=['Student UI','Node host','SDK MCP client','External servers','Claude model']
for n,(title,source,anchor,explanation,a,b) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');lines=text.splitlines();idx=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if anchor in l)
 count={1:3,2:6,3:5,4:5,5:4,6:5,7:3,8:5,9:6,10:3,11:6,12:3,13:3}.get(n,1);code='\n'.join(lines[idx:idx+count]).strip()
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language='typescript',explanation=explanation,firstLine=idx+1,lastLine=idx+count,anchors=[lines[idx].strip()],sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {n}. {explanation} This source excerpt shows the corresponding application statement.'))
 arrows.append([a,b,f'{n}. {title}'])
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
xs=[170,520,870,1220,1570];svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1740" height="1600" viewBox="0 0 1740 1600"><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#087fff"/></marker></defs><rect width="1740" height="1600" fill="#f4f9ff"/><text x="40" y="52" font-family="Arial" font-size="34" fill="#101a44">Lesson 24 · Declare → connect → approve external tools</text>']
