walk=''
for s in steps:walk+=f'<section class="step workflow-step" id="workflow-step-{s["number"]:02}"><span class="number">{s["number"]:02}</span><h3>{s["number"]}. {s["title"]}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">Source: {s["source"]} · lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]} · selected source; surrounding code omitted</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+'</section>'
document('/architecture.html','Architecture and <em>UML workflow.</em>','Every workflow step includes its corresponding coloured code excerpt.','<p class="note">This diagram groups setup and alternative experiments. Follow the selected mode and actual trace; one query does not execute every branch.</p><a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen external-MCP configuration and runtime workflow steps"></div>'+walk)
reference=[('Read the UML as alternative paths', 'The diagram groups setup and alternative experiments. Code declarations, project config and the permission comparisons are not all executed by every query. Follow the selected mode and its trace.'), ('Installed server instead of startup downloads', 'The app uses pinned @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem and invokes its installed entry point with Node. This avoids downloading an unpinned package at every run and handles Windows paths as separate arguments.'), ('Connection timing is version-dependent', 'The presentation summarizes connection waits. Current runtime behavior also depends on named servers, tool-search deferral and cached discovery. This app explicitly sets a 6000 ms first-turn wait and alwaysLoad, preserves init status and polls actual current status. The two-second wrapper delay is a labelled classroom experiment, not a claim about default startup duration.'), ('Availability is not approval', 'The visible namespace does not mean every call can execute. Exact approval and acceptEdits experiments record actual denials. No bypassPermissions mode is used. The docs wildcard in Combined still passes through a separate search-only host guard.'), ('Controlled project settings', 'The generated .mcp.json loads with settingSources: ["project"], enableAllProjectMcpServers and strictMcpConfig: false in that mode only. Other experiments use code-only declarations and strict MCP configuration. These settings do not modify your existing home configuration.'), ('Transport references', 'stdio uses a command and arguments; HTTP uses a URL. Legacy SSE and JSON streamable-http aliases are reference topics here, not live experiments. In-process SDK servers were taught in Lessons 22 and 23; no in-process server substitutes for the external servers in this app.'), ('Authentication and cached discovery', 'OAuth and private remote credentials belong to the next lesson. The public docs endpoint used here needs no remote service credential. Each classroom run uses fresh local runtime directories, so this app does not claim to benchmark warmed discovery caches or demonstrate every timeout default.'), ('Read-only classroom behavior', 'The filesystem process is restricted to its supplied root, and the host allows only directory listing. The docs host guard rejects feedback and other tools. Original fixture bytes are checked after the run. These controls describe this application; they are not an operating-system sandbox.')]

document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Thirteen source-linked steps connect declarations, status, permissions and real calls.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 24 · Connecting external MCP servers\n\nBased on Lesson24_Connecting_External_MCP_Servers.pptx. Five linked student pages with large text and coloured code in every UML step.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson24-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson24-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson24-external-mcp` instead of cloning. Open http://127.0.0.1:3124 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit, model access and internet are required. Windows may require Git Bash. No separate MCP server is needed.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nCopy .env.example only if .env does not exist. Enter your key privately and restart after edits. The startup script loads this file; existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo Managed Agents IDs are required. Real .env, media, private workspaces and dependencies are excluded from Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Selected source; surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Custom tools: official SDK documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/custom-tools)\n- [External MCP: official SDK documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/mcp)\n- [Official MCP servers](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. `npm test` checks classroom boundaries, server arguments, project config, approval selection and startup without paid model calls.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 24 student pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')
